From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [flutter/linux] fix ATK/glib C++ linkage on newer sysroots

fl_view_accessible.cc wraps <atk/atk.h> in an extern "C" block to give the
ATK functions C linkage. On newer sysroots (e.g. Debian trixie, glib >= 2.80)
ATK transitively includes glib's glib-typeof.h, which includes the C++
<type_traits> header. A C++ template header cannot be parsed inside an
extern "C" block, producing:

    error: templates must have C++ linkage

Removing the extern "C" wrapper instead breaks linking, since the ATK symbols
then get C++ linkage:

    ld.lld: error: undefined symbol: atk_get_major_version()

Include <glib.h> up front, outside the extern "C" block, so its include guards
prevent the C++ header from being re-parsed inside the block while the ATK
declarations keep their required C linkage.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [sysroot/glib version specific]

Signed-off-by: Joel Winarske <joel.winarske@gmail.com>
---
 .../shell/platform/linux/fl_view_accessible.cc          | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/linux/fl_view_accessible.cc b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/linux/fl_view_accessible.cc
--- a/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/linux/fl_view_accessible.cc
+++ b/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/linux/fl_view_accessible.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,12 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 // found in the LICENSE file.

+// ATK's headers pull in glib, whose glib-typeof.h includes the C++ <type_traits>
+// header (glib >= 2.80). That C++ header must not be parsed inside the extern "C"
+// block below, so include glib up front; its include guards then prevent it from
+// being re-read within the block.
+#include <glib.h>
+
 // Workaround missing C code compatibility in ATK header.
 // Fixed in https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/at-spi2-core/-/merge_requests/219
 extern "C" {
